    graph_review_letter:
      metadata:
        id: graph_review_letter
        name: "Subgraph: Review Letter"
        description: "Compliance review: flags letter statements that FACTS does not support."
      nodes:
        '[review_letter__prompt]:prompt "Prompt: User Message"':
          visualData: 420/40/420/1//
          data:
            type: user
            useTypeInput: false
            promptText: |-
              Review LETTER against FACTS.

              Flag as "major" any statement that:
              1. contradicts FACTS;
              2. adds an event, action, cause, status or condition that FACTS does not contain (for example saying an operation was executed or settled);
              3. drops or changes a condition, or the direction of a forecast (for example a rate that "may stop rising" described as a rate that "will fall");
              4. attributes a view to the wrong source, or presents a risk as a forecast;
              5. misspells or alters an asset or fund name;
              6. presents a since-purchase figure as a figure for the period, or the other way around.

              Flag as "minor" anything else a careful editor would fix (clumsy wording, repetition).

              Do not flag: figures copied correctly from FACTS; projections from FACTS.macro written with "deve", "tende a", "projeta" or "é projetado", because those words already mark a forecast; courtesy phrases; advisory opinions that follow directly from FACTS (such as the value of diversification or of staying aligned with the profile); framing such as "sugerimos avaliar".

              For each issue, excerpt is copied verbatim from LETTER, and problem explains in one English sentence what FACTS says instead. Return an empty list when there is nothing to flag.

              <facts>
              {{facts_json}}
              </facts>

              <letter>
              {{letter_json}}
              </letter>
            enableFunctionCall: false
          outgoingConnections:
            - 'output->"Chat: OpenAI (JSON Schema)" review_letter__chat/prompt'
